<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nanda dynasty</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nanda dynasty was a ruling house of the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magadha">Magadha</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the fourth century BCE. It controlled a large and wealthy state in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ganges-plain">Ganges</a> basin. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chandragupta-maurya">Chandragupta Maurya</a> overthrew the declining Nanda regime and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maurya-empire">Maurya Empire</a> in 321 BCE, inheriting its core territory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nanda-dynasty.jpg" alt="Nanda dynasty" width="320" height="299" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Avantiputra7 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Nanda_Empire,_c.325_BCE.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
